    ],
    "title": "Your title · Your role",
    "subtitle": "Outlook outage, explained"
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Microsoft_outage",
    "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/13/microsoft-hit-by-global-outages-what-happened-and-why",
    "https://controlplane.com/blog/post/microsoft-365-outage-november-2026-cause",
    "https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/12/tech/microsoft-outage-cripples-office-workers-nationwide"
  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "This week, Outlook stopped working around the world. But why?",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/outlook/campus.jpg",
            "tag": "Microsoft, Redmond · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: Coolcaesar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons",
            "kicker": "BREAKING",
            "headline": "Outlook down worldwide"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Thursday, people in more than 70 countries could not open their email.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "stat",
          "params": {
            "value": "70",
            "suffix": "+",
            "label": "countries could not use Outlook"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Teams and Copilot had problems too.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "list",
          "params": {
            "title": "What went down",
            "items": [
              "Outlook email",
              "Teams",
              "Copilot"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the UK, some hospitals cancelled operations and went back to paper.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/outlook/hospital.jpg",
            "tag": "UK hospital · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: David Hallam-Jones · CC BY-SA 2.0 · Wikimedia Commons",
            "kicker": "HOSPITALS HIT"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Courts, schools and governments were hit. Some traders went back to phones.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/outlook/trading.jpg",
            "tag": "Trading floor · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: Ank Kumar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "So what went wrong? It was not a cyberattack.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/outlook/racks.jpg",
            "tag": "Servers · file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: NOIRLab/NSF/AURA/T. Slovinský · CC BY 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons",
            "kicker": "WHY?"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Microsoft's email runs on many big computers called servers. They check their own health all the time.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "cascade",
          "params": {
            "stage": "ok",
            "title": "Email servers",
            "caption": "Health check: all OK"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Thursday, some servers failed this check, so they were switched off.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "cascade",
          "params": {
            "stage": "fail",
            "failed": 2,
            "title": "Health check failed",
            "caption": "Switched off"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The other servers had to do all their work. They got overloaded and stopped too, like dominoes.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "cascade",
          "params": {
            "stage": "domino",
            "failed": 2,
            "title": "Like dominoes",
            "caption": "Too much work → stopped too"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Microsoft says it still does not know what started it.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "title",
          "params": {
            "kicker": "STILL UNKNOWN",
            "text": "What started it?"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Engineers restarted servers and moved the traffic. Email came back slowly, after more than a day.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "timeline",
          "params": {
            "title": "Recovery",
            "items": [
              {
                "time": "Thu evening",
                "text": "Outlook goes down"
              },
              {
                "time": "Friday",
                "text": "Slow, partial recovery"
              },
              {
                "time": "Saturday",
                "text": "Email back to normal"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Experts say the world lost about 7 billion dollars of work.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "stat",
          "params": {
            "value": "7",
            "prefix": "$",
            "suffix": "B",
            "label": "of lost work (estimate)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When one big system breaks, the whole world feels it. Follow for more.",
      "graphics": [
        {
          "template": "photo",
          "params": {
            "src": "examples/assets/outlook/worker.jpg",
            "tag": "file photo",
            "credit": "Photo: Shixart1985 · CC BY 2.0 · Wikimedia Commons",
            "headline": "One system. The whole world."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}